  "original_question": "Compare IIT Bombay and IIT Madras in research performance in Engineering in 2025 and explain what RPC measures.",
  "answer": "### Research Performance Comparison: IIT Bombay vs. IIT Madras (2025)\n\nIn the 2025 Engineering category rankings, Indian Institute of Technology Madras demonstrates higher research performance compared to Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, specifically within the Research and Professional Practice (RPC) metric.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n* **RPC Score:** IIT Madras achieved an RPC score of 90.74, while IIT Bombay recorded a score of 84.81.\n* **Overall Ranking:** IIT Madras is ranked 1st overall in the Engineering category with a total score of 88.72, whereas IIT Bombay is ranked 3rd with a total score of 83.65.\n\n### Understanding the RPC Metric\nAccording to the official NIRF data dictionary, the **RPC (Research and Professional Practice)** score is a measure used to evaluate the research and professional practice performance of an institution [CITE-01]. It is recorded as a float value ranging from 0.00 to 100.00 [CITE-01].\n\n### Data Notes & Limitations\n* The analysis is based on a standard Top 100 publication cutoff.\n* The comparison is limited to the 2025 assessment year for the Engineering category.",
